# Resume PDF Render — Never Overwrite (ALWAYS)

When compiling any resume `.tex` under `harsh/resume/` (or any resume PDF elsewhere in this repo):

## Hard contract

1. **Never overwrite an existing PDF.** If a resume PDF already exists, do **not** write to that path again.
2. **One living LaTeX source:** `harsh/resume/HarshDesai_Resume.tex`. Edit that file in place. Do not edit files under `harsh/resume/archive/` unless reviving a frozen variant into a **new** named `.tex`.
3. PDF outputs are **append-only snapshots**. Put new renders in `harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/` with a **new, relevant filename**, for example:
   - `harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/HarshDesai_Resume_Instrumentation.pdf`
   - `harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/HarshDesai_Resume_Instrumentation_v2.pdf`
   - `harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/HarshDesai_YYYY-MM-DD_Resume_<focus>.pdf`
4. Prefer an explicit output path with `node generate-latex.mjs <input.tex> <new-output.pdf>`.
5. `generate-latex.mjs` refuses to overwrite unless `--force` is passed. Agents must **not** use `--force` except when the user explicitly asked to restore/replace a specific PDF.

## Wrong vs right

```text
❌ node generate-latex.mjs harsh/resume/HarshDesai_Resume.tex
   # writes HarshDesai_Resume.pdf next to the source — easy overwrite later

❌ node generate-latex.mjs harsh/resume/HarshDesai_Resume.tex harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/HarshDesai_Resume_UW-IDP_Mechanical-Instrumentationv3b.pdf
   # same path as an existing PDF

✅ node generate-latex.mjs harsh/resume/HarshDesai_Resume.tex harsh/resume/pdfs-from-living-source/HarshDesai_2026-08-13_Resume_Instrumentation.pdf
```

